{#- How each present character sounds: one block per NAMED entry that has an
    anchor. A nameless entry contributes nothing -- an unattributed anchor is
    the very defect this section exists to fix.

    Carries its OWN heading rather than sharing one with voice_examples.j2.
    The off-scene cast directory does share one, and used to pick its owner
    from DATA (`if not offscene_active`) while layout.py let a reader disable
    and reorder any section — so disabling one half lost the heading entirely
    (#423). Any data-derived "am I first?" test has that defect, because the
    question is about the merged, enabled layout. That directory now declares
    its heading as `Section.heading` and the render path places it; a section
    with a heading of its own, like this one, needs none of that machinery.

    Vars: cast_blocks. -#}
{%- set blocks = [] -%}
{%- for b in cast_blocks -%}
{%- if b.name and b.anchor -%}
{%- set _ = blocks.append("## " ~ b.name ~ "
" ~ b.anchor) -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- if blocks %}# Voice — how they sound

{{ blocks | join("

") }}
{%- endif -%}
